VidFlow UX Implementation Guide
What We're Building
VidFlow is a fully autonomous YouTube video production pipeline. User enters a video idea → system produces a complete video → publishes to YouTube.
The key insight: Topic in → Video out. Everything else is configuration.

Current State
Backend: ✅ Complete

All 6 nodes implemented (Trigger, Script, Voice, Thumbnail, Assembly, Publish)
Orchestrator with retry logic
Intervention framework
337 tests passing

UI: ❌ Shell only

Pages exist but no functional inputs
No node configuration panels
No pre-run flow
No intervention modals
"Run Pipeline" button shows alert('placeholder')


Core Philosophy
Automation First
The system should be able to run completely autonomously once configured:

User enters video idea
AI generates hooks, structure, script, titles, descriptions, tags
AI picks best options using scoring/ranking
AI generates voice, thumbnail, video
AI publishes (or saves as draft)

Intervention is Optional
Users can CHOOSE to pause and review at any point, but it's not required. Don't force clicks.
Configuration Lives in Nodes
Every setting lives inside its relevant node. No scattered settings pages. Click a node → see ALL its options.

