WARNINGS — Things That Will Go Wrong
1. Node Panel Complexity
Risk: Building 6 complex panels with dozens of tabs is a lot. Easy to get lost.
Prevention:

Build ONE node panel fully first (Script is most complex — start there)
Get it working end-to-end before building others
Use shared components (tab system, sliders, inputs)
Don't build all tabs at once — core tabs first, advanced later

2. State Sync Issues
Risk: Node config in UI gets out of sync with database
Prevention:

Single source of truth: database
Load config on panel open
Save on panel close or explicit save button
Optimistic UI with error rollback
Don't cache aggressively

3. WebSocket Complexity
Risk: WebSocket connections drop, events lost, UI doesn't update
Prevention:

Implement reconnection logic
Use event queue with sequence numbers
Fallback: poll endpoint if WebSocket fails
Test with slow connections

4. Intervention Modal Timing
Risk: Modal doesn't appear, appears at wrong time, or blocks forever
Prevention:

Clear state machine for run status
Test intervention flow extensively
Timeout handling — don't hang forever
Manual "check for intervention" button as fallback

5. Cost Estimation Drift
Risk: Estimated cost wildly different from actual cost
Prevention:

Use same calculation logic as execution
Update estimates when configs change
Show "estimate" clearly, not "price"
Log actual vs estimated for calibration

6. Voice Preview Performance
Risk: Preview requests spam API, cost money, slow UI
Prevention:

Debounce preview requests (500ms+)
Cache recent previews
Limit preview length (first 100 chars)
Show loading state

7. Template Bloat
Risk: Templates save too much data, become stale when node schemas change
Prevention:

Save minimal config (only non-default values)
Version template schema
Migration strategy for old templates
Validate template on load, warn if incompatible


DO NOT Do These Things
❌ Don't create new pages for each node
Node config panels are slide-overs/modals, NOT separate routes. User stays on Pipeline Editor.
❌ Don't make video idea optional
The system cannot run without knowing what video to make. Video idea is REQUIRED.
❌ Don't force intervention
Intervention points are opt-in checkboxes. Default is autonomous run.
❌ Don't auto-publish to Public by default
Default visibility MUST be Draft. User explicitly chooses to publish.
❌ Don't build a wizard flow
We discussed this and rejected it. Don't build step-by-step wizard. Build node panels + pre-run modal.
❌ Don't scatter settings
ALL settings for a node live in that node's panel. Don't put voice settings in a separate Voice Settings page.
❌ Don't ignore the Channel Bible
Script node MUST load and use Channel Bible. It's not optional decoration.
❌ Don't skip error states
Every async operation needs: loading state, success state, error state with message.
❌ Don't build without types
All configs, API responses, WebSocket events must be typed. Use Zod schemas already in codebase.
❌ Don't break existing tests
337 tests exist. They should still pass. Run tests frequently.
❌ Don't output code to CLI
Large files will hit rate limits. Use file creation tools, not console output.

